SOAPBOX: Improved antennas could not make up for poor progation: K3LR arrays for 160 & 80m, 40m 1/2wave vertical, a large rhombic (nw-se) and quads (ne-sw) for the upper bands, plus various rx antennas. Tx: Alinco DX70 with extra cooling: a wind & solar powered off-grid setup in a remote spot on the western edge of Europe - no qrm. 10m gave a few hours each day with poor signals to South America, Asia was rarely heard on all bands, Topband had few U.S. visitors. K3LR and K1LZ produced outstanding signals on 80 &160m.
SOAPBOX: There should be a time limit on single ops: trying to reach a total of 48 hours is a health hazard.
SOAPBOX: Stefan Ei4KU
